        "created_at": "2026-02-14T09:29:05.572Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone!</p>\n<p>If anyone is using copilot or claude for helping them develop their addon/macros I have created an agent with the entire 12.x API as skills. I created it to help me convert some legacy mods that I wanted to modern wow.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubrepo\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/JBurlison/WoWAddonAPIAgents\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/JBurlison/WoWAddonAPIAgents\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n  <img width=\"695\" height=\"347\" src=\"https://opengraph.githubassets.com/bdf406ff22f6c278ad090fd11a49f4aa/JBurlison/WoWAddonAPIAgents\" class=\"thumbnail\">\n\n  <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/JBurlison/WoWAddonAPIAgents\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GitHub - JBurlison/WoWAddonAPIAgents: Entire suite of VS Code Copilot agents, skills,...</a></h3>\n\n    <p><span class=\"github-repo-description\">Entire suite of VS Code Copilot agents, skills, instructions and prompts for creating modern wow addons </span></p>\n</div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n",
